@startuml
title Tuna <-> MQTT <-> Store Controller (POS) Host Sync

autonumber
skinparam backgroundColor #FAFAF7
skinparam sequence {
	ArrowColor #2D5B87
	LifeLineBorderColor #2D5B87
	LifeLineBackgroundColor #F1F6FB
	ParticipantBorderColor #355E3B
	ParticipantBackgroundColor #EEF6EE
	ParticipantFontColor #1F2A1F
}

actor "Tech/Process" as Tech
participant "TUNA" as TUNA
participant "MQTT Broker" as MQTT
participant "Store Controller\n(POS)" as POS

note over TUNA,POS
Host sync no longer depends on ISP for file processing.
TUNA notifies by MQTT, then POS downloads files via REST and processes locally.
end note

== Change Trigger ==
Tech -> TUNA: Makes changes in TUNA
TUNA -> TUNA: Build latest hosts, resolv, and bootptab payload

== Notification Layer ==
TUNA -> MQTT: Publish host-sync notification\n(topic: store/<id>/hostsync)
MQTT -> POS: Deliver host-sync notification

== Controller Pulls Files ==
POS -> TUNA: REST GET /hostsync/hosts
TUNA --> POS: hosts file
POS -> TUNA: REST GET /hostsync/resolv
TUNA --> POS: resolv file
POS -> TUNA: REST GET /hostsync/bootptab
TUNA --> POS: bootptab file

== Controller Local Processing ==
POS -> POS: Validate and stage downloaded files
POS -> POS: Extract LANE assignments and adxautonet entries
POS -> POS: Remove xx and DHCP entries from hosts
POS -> POS: Add MAC addresses as comments
POS -> POS: Reinsert adxautonet entries
POS -> POS: Apply resolv and final hosts file locally

note over POS
All heavy lifting is now performed on the controller.
end note

@enduml

